        },
        "summary_en": {
          "motivation": "To investigate the formation of crystallographic texture in selective laser melted NiTi alloy and its effect on mechanical anisotropy.",
          "method": "Electron backscatter diffraction (EBSD) was used to characterize texture, and tensile and compression tests were performed to evaluate anisotropy.",
          "result": "The study demonstrated that SLM process parameters significantly influence texture type and the degree of mechanical anisotropy.",
          "validation": "Experimental validation through microstructural characterization and mechanical testing."
